# User-facing flows

`docs/flows.md` is the operator-visible order of `npm run dev`, `npm run sync`, and `npm run ui`. When that order changes, update `docs/flows.md` in the same change. A refactor that keeps the order leaves the file as it is.

Update the diagrams when the operator would see a different sequence. Examples: polling after inspect instead of before it, dropping the Telegram alert after a sent application, or filling an expose refresh inside the progress page instead of on the next agent tick.

Leave the diagrams when the sequence the operator sees stays the same. Examples: a new recovery action, a different selector, or a renamed private helper.
